    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The last resident, 87‑year‑old Lawrence Mitchner, left the village on April 20, 1973, marking the end of New Burlington’s original community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://warrencountypost.com/g/waynesville-oh/n/138247/remembering-village-no-more"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Village limits once stretched across parts of Spring Valley Township in Greene County and Chester Township in Clinton County, while a planned dam was being built just south in Warren County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://warrencountypost.com/g/waynesville-oh/n/138247/remembering-village-no-more"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The old Methodist Church was the last place a marriage took place in New Burlington before the town was abandoned.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://warrencountypost.com/g/waynesville-oh/n/138247/remembering-village-no-more"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In spring 1973, only four structures remained: the cobbler’s shop, the Quaker church, and two houses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://warrencountypost.com/g/waynesville-oh/n/138247/remembering-village-no-more"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Lake planners originally intended the reservoir to extend north up Route 380 to Spring Valley Paintersville Road, but that section was later dropped.",
